WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:18.110
morning Swallow was eager to catch up to the flock.

2
00:00:19.471 --> 00:00:21.872
He flew up to say good-bye to the statue.

3
00:00:21.892 --> 00:00:26.534
"Thank you for keeping me warm last night," he said.

4
00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:30.535
The statue sighed.

5
00:00:30.555 --> 00:00:32.136
"You're welcome.

6
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.101
Thank you for listening to my sad story."

7
00:00:36.121 --> 00:00:41.082
"I hope you find a way to be happy," Swallow said.

8
00:00:41.102 --> 00:00:46.784
"I won't—not until everyone has what he or she needs."

9
00:00:49.665 --> 00:00:52.746
Swallow never had to think about what anyone else needed.

10
00:00:53.906 --> 00:00:55.207
The flock leader did that.

11
00:00:56.747 --> 00:00:58.468
Leader looked after all the birds.

12
00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:04.149
"Too bad there's nothing you can do," Swallow said.

13
00:01:04.169 --> 00:01:09.070
"There are things that I could do," the statue said.

14
00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.571
"If only I could move."

15
00:01:14.492 --> 00:01:16.332
Perhaps the swallow should have left then.

16
00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:20.774
But he had been thinking about the statue's unhappiness.

17
00:01:22.194 --> 00:01:25.035
He had been thinking about the townspeople's misery too.

18
00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:28.076
"Tell me your idea, Prince."

19
00:01:33.308 --> 00:01:35.029
Swallow listened carefully.

20
00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:38.310
"You're sure you want to do this?"

21
00:01:41.932 --> 00:01:44.673
"Okay," Swallow said.

22
00:01:44.693 --> 00:01:48.815
"First, I'll do what you asked.

23
00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:50.635
Then I'll leave for Egypt.

24
00:01:51.696 --> 00:01:53.036
I hope this will make you happier."

25
00:01:53.056 --> 00:01:56.098
"Thank you, Swallow."

26
00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:01.400
Swallow flew down to the statue's belt.

27
00:02:03.544 --> 00:02:07.246
He gripped one of the rubies with his beak and pulled.

28
00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:11.349
Then he flew off, carrying the jewel.

29
00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.131
Swallow flew to the edge of town.

30
00:02:16.632 --> 00:02:19.293
He soon spotted where the statue had told him to go.

31
00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.976
It was a one-room house.

32
00:02:26.097 --> 00:02:27.017
He looked inside.

33
00:02:28.438 --> 00:02:31.220
The room was empty except for a table and bed.

34
00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.289
A woman sat at the table sewing a dress.

35
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.230
But this wasn't just any dress.

36
00:02:39.631 --> 00:02:43.613
It was a beautiful ballgown covered in shiny crystals.

37
00:02:46.134 --> 00:02:47.535
Swallow gasped.

38
00:02:47.555 --> 00:02:49.615
"That's stunning!

39
00:02:50.616 --> 00:02:51.856
She doesn't need this jewel.

40
00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:56.479
I'll return it to the statue and then leave for Egypt!"

41
00:02:57.559 --> 00:03:00.680
Swallow hopped to the edge of the windowsill.

42
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.363
He was about to take flight when someone began coughing.

43
00:03:07.926 --> 00:03:09.207
Swallow looked closer.

44
00:03:09.227 --> 00:03:11.469
It was a little boy.

45
00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:14.531
He looked very sick.

46
00:03:14.552 --> 00:03:18.495
"My poor baby," the woman said.

47
00:03:18.515 --> 00:03:21.898
"We will have money for medicine soon.

48
00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:26.361
As soon as I finish this ballgown for a lady."

49
00:03:26.381 --> 00:03:31.877
"Oh!" Swallow realized.

50
00:03:31.897 --> 00:03:35.979
"The seamstress is making the dress for someone else.

51
00:03:37.219 --> 00:03:39.020
She really does need this jewel."

52
00:03:41.541 --> 00:03:46.363
Whoosh! Swallow zoomed inside and dropped the jewel in the woman's lap.

53
00:03:48.264 --> 00:03:50.565
Then he flew out the window before she could see him.

54
00:03:53.286 --> 00:03:54.667
The woman gasped.

55
00:03:54.687 --> 00:03:57.608
"A gift from above!

56
00:03:59.997 --> 00:04:01.322
It seems impossible.

57
00:04:02.045 --> 00:04:05.218
But now I can buy my boy his medicine!"
